---
/**
 * Honest "closed" page for a plan-gated tenant (API 402 storefront_disabled).
 *
 * Distinct on purpose from the "temporarily unavailable … try again in a
 * minute" outage fallback: that copy told shoppers of a gated shop to keep
 * retrying something that will never come back on its own. This is the
 * durable state — the owner's package lapsed — so say so plainly, with a
 * quiet renewal hint for the owner who lands on their own site.
 */
---

<div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 py-16 text-center">
  <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">This shop is currently closed</h1>
  <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-500">
    The online store is offline for now. Please check back later, or reach the
    shop through its Facebook page.
  </p>
  {/* "after the next update", not "back online now": this page is BAKED into
      the prerendered build, and nothing rebuilds the storefront on plan
      renewal yet — a tenant who just paid may still be looking at it. */}
  <p class="mt-6 text-xs text-slate-400">
    Shop owner? Renew your subscription from your dashboard; the site comes
    back online after the next update.
  </p>
</div>
